            <ArticleTitle>Headache attributed to airplane travel (&quot;airplane headache&quot;): first Italian case.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>196-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A new form of headache, whose attacks seem to be stereotyped, has been recently reported; because of the peculiarity of its onset, strictly related to airplane travel, the name of &quot;Airplane headache&quot; was proposed. A total of 7 cases have been published. Here we present the first Italian one. Furthermore the revision of the clinical characteristics of each patient leads us to propose provisional diagnostic criteria.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
